Native KV capacity env: no upstream code is copied or adapted. Upstream
validates scheduler capacity configuration at construction and raises on an
out-of-range value; the listed pull requests extend that to non-positive
capacities. Fak keeps its documented ignore-and-fall-back policy for a
malformed FAK_NATIVE_KV_MAX_BLOCKS or FAK_NATIVE_KV_BLOCK_TOKENS (preemption
stays off, blocks stay 16 tokens) and now reports each ignored value, with the
fallback it took, as a typed error, a one-line [fak] stderr notice when the
native scheduler is built, and a native-kv-env warning in the fak serve startup
messages, so an operator's intended setting is no longer replaced silently.
